{"book":10,"chapter":22,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / THE LANGUAGE IN DEPTH / CHAPTER 22","slides":[{"title":"One tool instead of a set","sub":"Chapter 22 · cargo","short":"Introduction","main":"cargo builds, runs, tests and pulls dependencies; the layout is the same for everyone.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python: a set of tools","Rust: cargo","One layout"],"captions":["In Python a project is venv, pip, pytest, black, mypy and a config for each","In Rust cargo does it all: creates a project, builds, runs, tests, formats and downloads dependencies","The layout is the same in every project: Cargo.toml, src/, tests/ — open someone's repo and you know where things are"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"venv","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":116.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pip","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":182.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pytest","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":248.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"black","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a4","x":314.0,"y":70.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"mypy","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"each tool — its own config","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"cargo","tone":"green","size":14.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":50.0,"y":120.0,"w":58.0,"h":26.0,"text":"build","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":116.0,"y":120.0,"w":58.0,"h":26.0,"text":"run","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":182.0,"y":120.0,"w":58.0,"h":26.0,"text":"test","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":248.0,"y":120.0,"w":58.0,"h":26.0,"text":"fmt","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b4","x":314.0,"y":120.0,"w":58.0,"h":26.0,"text":"doc","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e0","x1":140.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":50.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":160.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":116.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":180.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":182.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":200.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":248.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":220.0,"y1":68.0,"x2":314.0,"y2":106.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"t","x":30.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["my_app/","├── Cargo.toml","├── Cargo.lock","├── src/","│   ├── main.rs","│   └── lib.rs","└── tests/"],"hl":[1,3,6],"lang":"plain","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":200.0}]],"cues":[15.7,25.6]}]},{"title":"cargo commands","sub":"build, check, test, release","short":"cargo","main":"check is faster than build; release optimizes, debug checks overflow.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["new, build, run","check, test, fmt","debug and release"],"captions":["cargo new creates a package; build compiles; run compiles and runs; the result sits in target/","check only verifies types (fast), test runs tests, fmt unifies the style, clippy looks for suspicious code","A debug build is fast and checks overflow; a release build is optimized — like -O0 and -O3 in a C compiler"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ cargo new hello","$ cd hello","$ cargo run","   Compiling hello v0.1.0","Hello, world!"],"hl":[2],"lang":"plain","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":60.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"check","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":116.0,"y":60.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"test","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":182.0,"y":60.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"fmt","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":248.0,"y":60.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"clippy","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a4","x":314.0,"y":60.0,"w":58.0,"h":28.0,"text":"doc","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"check: types without code generation","size":9.5},{"t":"text","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"several times faster than build","tone":"green","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"debug (default)","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"--release","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"bar","id":"b1","x":90.0,"y":124.0,"w":40.0,"hh":16.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"yellow","text":""},{"t":"bar","id":"b2","x":270.0,"y":124.0,"w":40.0,"hh":70.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"green","text":""},{"t":"text","id":"l","x":180.0,"y":144.0,"text":"program speed","size":9.0}]],"cues":[13.1,24.6]}]},{"title":"Modules and paths","sub":"crate, self, super, use","short":"Modules","main":"A crate is a tree of modules; a path starts from crate, self or super.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Module tree","Paths","use"],"captions":["A crate is a tree of modules: mod declares a module, its contents sit in braces or in a file of the same name","A path starts at the root (crate::), at the current module (self::) or at the parent (super::)","use brings a name into scope; as renames, braces pull in several names"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"crate","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"net","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":260.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":24.0,"text":"db","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":60.0,"y":130.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"tcp","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":150.0,"y":130.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"udp","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":42.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":68.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":42.0,"x2":240.0,"y2":68.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":80.0,"y1":92.0,"x2":64.0,"y2":120.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e4","x1":120.0,"y1":92.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":120.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["crate::net::tcp::connect()","self::helper()","super::config::load()"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};","use std::fmt::Result as FmtResult;","use crate::net::tcp::*;"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[10.6,30.5]}]},{"title":"Visibility","sub":"pub, pub(crate), fields","short":"Visibility","main":"Private by default; private fields make the constructor the guardian of invariants.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Private by default","pub variants","Invariants"],"captions":["Whatever is not marked pub is visible only inside its module and its descendants","pub — to everyone, pub(crate) — inside the crate, pub(super) — to the parent; struct fields are closed separately","A private field = the struct cannot be built bypassing the constructor, so the constructor guarantees the invariant"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["mod bank {","    fn audit() {}            // private","    pub fn deposit() {}       // public","}","bank::deposit();  // ok","bank::audit();    // ✕ E0603"],"hl":[5],"bad":[5],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"v0","x":90.0,"y":36.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"pub — everyone","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v1","x":90.0,"y":68.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"pub(crate) — crate","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v2","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"pub(super) — the parent","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v3","x":90.0,"y":132.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"(none) — module+kids","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["pub struct Percent(u8);   // field is private","impl Percent {","    pub fn new(n: u8) -> Option<Percent> {","        (n <= 100).then(|| Percent(n))","    }","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[13.9,27.5]}]},{"title":"Re-export","sub":"pub use and prelude","short":"pub use","main":"pub use gives a short public path and hides the internal structure.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Deep paths","pub use","Prelude"],"captions":["Without a re-export the user would have to write a long chain: mylib::shapes::circle::Circle","pub use shapes::circle::Circle; — the type is reachable shortly: mylib::Circle, and the internal layout stays your business","Frequently used items go into a prelude and are imported in one line: use mylib::prelude::*;"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["use mylib::shapes::circle::Circle;","use mylib::shapes::rect::Rect;"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"leaking the internal structure","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["// lib.rs","mod shapes;                // private","pub use shapes::circle::Circle;","pub use shapes::rect::Rect;"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"use mylib::{Circle, Rect};","tone":"green","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["pub mod prelude {","    pub use crate::{Circle, Rect, Shape};","}","use mylib::prelude::*;"],"hl":[3],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[7.0,21.5]}]},{"title":"Dependencies","sub":"Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, features","short":"Dependencies","main":"Compatible versions, exact lock, and features for extra code.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Cargo.toml","Cargo.lock","Features"],"captions":["serde = \"1.0\" — “any compatible starting from 1.0”; cargo picks the newest from the 1.x line","Cargo.lock keeps exact versions, so every build is the same; for applications it is committed","features turn on the needed code: serde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] } — the rest is not built"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["[package]","name = \"hello\"","version = \"0.1.0\"","edition = \"2021\"","","[dependencies]","serde = \"1.0\"","rand = \"0.8\""],"hl":[6,7],"lang":"plain","size":10.0,"lh":15.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["[[package]]","name = \"serde\"","version = \"1.0.203\"","checksum = \"a3f5…\""],"hl":[2],"lang":"plain","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":128.0,"text":"exact version and hash: reproducible","tone":"green","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["[dependencies]","serde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }","","[dev-dependencies]","tempfile = \"3\"   # for tests only"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"plain","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[6.8,28.6]}]},{"title":"Documentation","sub":"/// and doc tests","short":"Documentation","main":"Examples in comments run as tests.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["/// comment","Doc test","cargo doc"],"captions":["Three slashes document an item; //! describes the whole module or crate","A code block inside a comment runs as a real test with cargo test: documentation does not go stale silently","cargo doc builds pages like docs.rs: signatures, examples and links are visible"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["/// Returns the sum of two numbers.","///","/// # Panics","/// Does not panic.","pub fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { a + b }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["/// ```","/// assert_eq!(mylib::add(2, 3), 5);","/// ```","pub fn add(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32 { ... }","// cargo test → Doc-tests mylib ... ok"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":56.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"///\ncomments","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":120.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":200.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"target/doc/\nHTML pages","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"cargo doc --open","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[11.5,21.8]}]},{"title":"Unit tests","sub":"#[test], assert, should_panic","short":"Unit","main":"Tests sit next to the code and see the parent's private items.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["#[cfg(test)]","assert macros","should_panic and Result"],"captions":["Tests sit next to the code in a tests module; the cfg(test) attribute turns it on only for cargo test","assert! checks a condition, assert_eq! and assert_ne! show both sides on failure","#[should_panic] expects a panic; a test may return Result and use ? — then Err means failure"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#[cfg(test)]","mod tests {","    use super::*;","    #[test]","    fn adds() { assert_eq!(add(2, 3), 5); }","}"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["assert!(is_even(4));","assert_eq!(add(2, 2), 4);","assert_ne!(add(2, 2), 5);","// left: 5  right: 4   ← on failure"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#[test]","#[should_panic(expected = \"division by zero\")]","fn div_by_zero() { div(1, 0); }","#[test]","fn parses() -> Result<(), ParseIntError> {","    assert_eq!(\"7\".parse::<i32>()?, 7);","    Ok(())","}"],"hl":[1,4],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":15.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[13.1,25.7]}]},{"title":"Integration tests","sub":"tests/ and a thin main","short":"Integration","main":"Each file in tests/ is a client crate: only pub items are visible.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["tests/ folder","Client crate","lib + thin main"],"captions":["Each file in tests/ is a separate crate: it links the library as an outside user","So only pub items are visible: the contract is tested the way a user will see it","The executable crate is kept thin: main calls the library, and all the logic is covered by library tests"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["my_app/","├── src/lib.rs","├── src/main.rs","└── tests/","    ├── api.rs","    └── common/mod.rs"],"hl":[3,4,5],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":220.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"text":"test file =\nseparate crate","tone":"green","size":9.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":80.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"tests/api.rs","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"mylib\n(pub only)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"use mylib::add;  — like a user","size":9.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"main.rs\n3 lines","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":116.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":196.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":280.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":44.0,"text":"lib.rs\nall logic\n+ tests","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.8,30.0]}]},{"title":"Good tests","sub":"Boundaries and mutations","short":"Good tests","main":"Boundaries, a table of cases, and a deliberately broken implementation.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Arrange–act–assert","Table of cases","Break and check"],"captions":["Prepare the data, perform the action, check the result: three parts, one meaningful check per test","A table of “input → expected” pairs runs in one loop; boundaries matter most: empty, zero, maximum, negative","Mutation check: deliberately break the implementation — at least one test must turn red"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let mut s = Stack::new();      // arrange","s.push(1);                     // act","assert_eq!(s.pop(), Some(1));  // assert"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let cases = [(0, 0), (1, 1), (-1, 1),","             (i32::MAX, i32::MAX)];","for (x, want) in cases {","    assert_eq!(abs(x), want);","}"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"g","x":100.0,"y":50.0,"w":150.0,"h":26.0,"text":"correct implementation: 0 failures","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":90.0,"y":90.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"mutant: abs → x","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":280.0,"y":90.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"failures ≥ 1","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":90.0,"x2":224.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"tests that never turn red are not tests","size":9.5}]],"cues":[14.4,26.3]}]},{"title":"Library errors","sub":"Error, source, non_exhaustive","short":"Errors","main":"Your own enum, Display, Error, From; panic only on a contract violation.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Error enum","source()","non_exhaustive"],"captions":["A public function returns Result with its own enum: Display for people, Error for the ecosystem, From for ?","The source() method returns the cause — this builds chains like “failed to read config: invalid number”","#[non_exhaustive] lets you add variants later without breaking compatibility; panic only on a contract violation"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#[derive(Debug)]","pub enum ConfigError {","    Missing(String),","    BadNumber(ParseIntError),","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ConfigError","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":120.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":200.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ParseIntError\n(cause)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"err.source()","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#[non_exhaustive]","pub enum Error { A, B }","// clients must write _ => …","// → C can be added without a major release"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[14.4,28.4]}]},{"title":"cfg, const and globals","sub":"Conditional compilation","short":"cfg","main":"cfg and const fn are evaluated at build time; globals go through atomics and OnceLock.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["cfg","const fn","Atomics and OnceLock"],"captions":["#[cfg(...)] and cfg!(...) pick code for the OS, word size, build mode or feature — the rest is not even compiled","const fn and const are evaluated at build time: a table of squares sits right in the executable","A global counter is AtomicUsize; a value to create once is OnceLock; mutable statics need unsafe"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]","fn sep() -> char { '/' }","if cfg!(debug_assertions) { /* debug */ }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const fn sq(x: u32) -> u32 { x * x }","const TABLE: [u32; 4] = [sq(1), sq(2), sq(3), sq(4)];","// 1, 4, 9, 16 — in .rodata"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["static NEXT: AtomicUsize = AtomicUsize::new(0);","fn id() -> usize { NEXT.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed) }","static CFG: OnceLock<String> = OnceLock::new();"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[11.4,21.0]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next — threads and shared state.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Project","Quality","Next"],"captions":["cargo — one tool for everything; crates and modules with private-by-default visibility; pub use shapes the interface","Versions and features manage dependencies, documentation runs as tests, and good tests catch a broken implementation","Next — threads and shared state: Mutex, channels, Arc and data races"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"cargo","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"crates\nand modules","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"pub use","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"versions\nand features","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"doc tests","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"mutations","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"thread","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Mutex\nArc","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"channels","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.0,18.1]}]}]}